## Post-sweep order (laptop, mortcal-cpu env) — read results only at step 7

1. `bash scripts/server_pull.sh shift placebo` (pulls parquet + parts + logs; purges local snapshots first)
2. `python scripts/final_qa.py results/shift.parquet results/shift_gp.parquet results/placebo.parquet results/placebo_gp.parquet` → must print QA PASS (machine=0)
3. `python scripts/analyse.py results/shift.parquet results/shift_gp.parquet --out results/shift_analysis.json` (and placebo)
4. `python scripts/sensitivities.py ...` → `results/sensitivities.json`
5. `python scripts/make_tables.py --parquet ... (all four) --analysis ... --sensitivities results/sensitivities.json --out paper/tables --final`
6. `python scripts/make_figures.py ...` → `paper/figures`
7. compile: copy `paper/` to the scratchpad, `env -u ALL_PROXY <scratchpad>/tectonic/tectonic.exe -X compile --keep-logs main.tex`; check `grep -c '^!' main.log` = 0 and no "Float too large".
Then commit the generated tables/figures deliberately (they are gitignored until final).

## Rules that are easy to break

- Real-data runs need `allow_real=True` (the CLI passes it) — the auditable act.
- Never clip SVAR rates or Poisson means (addendum 3 §7): rejection only. The
  rejection FIRES on real data (TWN 990–1000/1000 draws explosive; pboot
  overflows on the longest panels) — that is a finding, recorded as
  method-failure rows, reported in tab-infeasible.
- Losses are never imputed: `mortcal.inference` raises on non-finite input and
  on any attempt to rank conformal cells' placeholder crps/logscore — conformal
  contrasts use `winkler95` (interval score). CBD (45 ages) never enters a
  ranking with 100-age families.
- Conformal cells have NO derived-quantity intervals (e0/e65/ä65 → n/a).
- One device per regime; `device` column records it (all CPU so far).
- Do NOT resume workflow `wf_75bb90b5-839` (dead; clobbers manual fixes).
- Do not commit `results/parity/D_*.csv` / `E_*.csv` (raw HMD) or any
  snapshot-derived number into .tex/.md. `results/_*` are local snapshots.
- `pkill -f <pattern>` from an `ssh host "..."` one-liner matches the caller's
  own command line — use `scripts/server_relaunch.sh` (bracket patterns).
- `Start-Process -ArgumentList` joins elements without quoting — launch bash
  via a wrapper script in a space-free path.

## Environment traps (cost real time)

- Windows: 12 workers importing the CUDA torch exceed the commit limit
  (WinError 1455) — that is why sweeps left the laptop. Git Bash heredocs with
  apostrophes/backslashes mangle — use the Write/Edit tools for files.
- `uv sync` with torch: a killed sync leaves zombie uv.exe holding `.venv`.
- Thread pinning belongs in the launch ENV, not a multiprocessing initializer
  (OpenBLAS reads it at import; measured load 52 → 11).

